1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:01,830
♪

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:04,500
[ANNE]
Wake up! Mythril Lid Pod!

3
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:06,920
Ah, what now?

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,880
[ANNE]
I got to see Challe yesterday!

5
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:11,170
[gasps] Did you, really?

6
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:14,460
And when I told him that
I'll be able to set him free

7
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:16,290
if I'm successful
at my job here,

8
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:17,750
he said he would wait for me!

9
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:20,540
[MYTHRIL]
He did? That's wonderful!

10
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:23,250
I thought he'd say, "Go away,
I don't need your help,"

11
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,790
so this is a surprise!

12
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:26,080
[gasps]

13
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:27,460
Having to be
that girl's companion

14
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:29,330
must really be unbearable.

15
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,880
She might be making him
do sordid things

16
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:33,420
we can't even imagine.

17
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,630
Um, what do you mean by sordid?

18
00:00:35,710 --> 00:00:36,920
Don't worry about it!

19
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,670
[grunts]

20
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:41,330
Let's rebuild this place
as quickly as we can

21
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:43,420
and then rescue
Challe Fen Challe!

22
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,460
[ANNE]
Oh, right.

23
00:02:16,330 --> 00:02:18,540
[birds chirping]

24
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,330
[men gasp]

25
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:22,330
Hmm.

26
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,670
- [NADIR] A girl.
- [Anne gasps]

27
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:26,080
And a fairy too!

28
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:28,170
[yelps]
What's your problem?

29
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:30,000
- [grunts]
- [NADIR] Hey, come out!

30
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,540
I've never seen a fairy
as small as you!

31
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:33,040
Let me look at you!
Please? Please?

32
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:34,920
Easy, Nadir.
That's quite enough.

33
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,710
Ah! Looks like everyone's here.

34
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:40,080
♪

35
00:02:40,170 --> 00:02:42,250
Aren't you going to
introduce us, Elliot?

36
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:43,880
I was about to.

37
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,420
This is Anne Halford.

38
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,580
Starting today,
she'll be working here

39
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:50,040
as our very own
Head of Artisans.

40
00:02:50,130 --> 00:02:51,250
And...

41
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:57,000
this fairy is her helper,
Mythril Lid Pod.

42
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:57,920
[grunts]

43
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,040
- Hmm?
- [KING] Wait, Halford?

44
00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:02,750
The one who made a confection
for the former Duke of Philax?

45
00:03:02,830 --> 00:03:04,580
- [Mythril whimpers]
- [ELLIOT] One and the same!

46
00:03:04,670 --> 00:03:06,000
And, as of this year,

47
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:08,040
she's become
a silver sugar master!

48
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,210
Are you serious?

49
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:12,630
But why would someone so amazing
work here?

50
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:14,250
And she's a girl, at that!

51
00:03:14,330 --> 00:03:16,920
[gasps and sighs]

52
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,960
[KING]
So, Mr. Glen approved this?

53
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,170
Yes.

54
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:21,540
[KING] Then who am I to object?

55
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:25,380
Hello, there. My name is King.

56
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:27,040
That's your name?

57
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:29,670
Well, I forgot my real name
some time ago.

58
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:32,500
I see.
It's an honor to meet you, King.

59
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:34,880
Huh? What's this?

60
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:37,750
Huh? A handshake?

61
00:03:37,830 --> 00:03:40,630
[KING]
Oh. Yes, of course! A handshake!

62
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:42,540
[King grunts]

63
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:44,670
Uh...

64
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:48,250
And my name's Nadir.
So, will you come out now?

65
00:03:48,330 --> 00:03:50,420
- [MYTHRIL] No!
- Mm...

66
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:54,790
A wise decision, little fairy.
My name is Valentine.

67
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:56,630
It's lovely to meet you.

68
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:58,580
[ANNE] Nice to meet you, too.

69
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:01,130
[ELLIOT]
Oh, Orland's here! Perfect!

70
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,710
So, now that you've met
all five of our workers,

71
00:04:06,790 --> 00:04:09,460
we're at your service,
Miss Head of Artisans!

72
00:04:11,130 --> 00:04:11,960
[chuckles]

73
00:04:14,290 --> 00:04:15,580
[ANNE] Let's see.

74
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:17,330
- Where to start?
- Hey.

75
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:19,080
[ANNE] Oh, dear,

76
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:20,670
I don't really have
a clear understanding

77
00:04:20,750 --> 00:04:22,040
of what I've agreed to.

78
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:24,170
Um, for now,

79
00:04:24,250 --> 00:04:26,420
please continue your work
from yesterday.

80
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,710
- [NADIR] Sure!
- [KING] Will do.

81
00:04:28,250 --> 00:04:29,880
- [ORLAND] Hmm.
- [VALENTINE] Right.

82
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:33,250
[metal clatters]

83
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:35,380
[Anne sighs]

84
00:04:36,290 --> 00:04:38,330
Anne, what should I do?

85
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:39,710
Perhaps you could

86
00:04:39,790 --> 00:04:41,500
get a little bit
of the cleaning done?

87
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,250
Leave it to me! [grunts]

88
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:44,920
[ANNE]
In the meantime,

89
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,630
I'll assess the situation!

90
00:04:48,250 --> 00:04:49,080
♪

91
00:04:49,170 --> 00:04:52,130
My, he's very talented.

92
00:04:52,210 --> 00:04:53,670
Mr. Langston,

93
00:04:53,750 --> 00:04:56,130
what sort of commission are you
working on at the moment?

94
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:58,330
Hm?

95
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:01,580
Don't bother
with the formalities.

96
00:05:01,670 --> 00:05:03,540
There's no need to say Mr.

97
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:06,790
Oh. All right then.

98
00:05:07,830 --> 00:05:09,290
So, what's that?

99
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,500
[ORLAND]
It's an order from a shop owner.

100
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:13,920
Apparently,
it's for their son's birthday.

101
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,250
[ANNE]
I see, so the son likes horses?

102
00:05:16,330 --> 00:05:17,830
[ORLAND]
I wouldn't know.

103
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:20,960
I suggested a few ideas
and they chose a horse.

104
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:22,960
[ANNE] Did they say why?

105
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:25,170
[ORLAND]
Was I supposed to ask them?

106
00:05:25,250 --> 00:05:27,170
[ANNE] There may be something
they'd like better.

107
00:05:27,250 --> 00:05:30,290
Or perhaps there's a specific
type of horse they'd prefer.

108
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:31,960
[ORLAND] Honoring
the customer's every whim

109
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,130
doesn't always make
for a quality product.

110
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,670
[gasps]

111
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:39,330
[ORLAND] We employ all of our
skill to make what speaks to us.

112
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:41,630
Otherwise,
we can't create anything good.

113
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:45,170
[ANNE] I always thought giving
the customer what they want

114
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:46,790
was the best way.

115
00:05:47,630 --> 00:05:50,500
♪

116
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:52,460
[gasps]

117
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,630
- It's lovely!
- [gasps]

118
00:05:54,670 --> 00:05:55,830
The color is so nice!

119
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:58,330
Ah! You don't have to get
so close, you know!

120
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:00,920
Huh? Oh, pardon me!

121
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:04,250
[NADIR] Maybe Anne should start
wearing men's clothes.

122
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:06,750
Maybe I should punch you.

123
00:06:06,830 --> 00:06:09,460
[ANNE] It seems like
he's uncomfortable around women.

124
00:06:10,330 --> 00:06:12,170
- [VALENTINE] Excuse me.
- Yes?

125
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:13,960
[VALENTINE] I've finished
maintenance on the tools.

126
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:14,880
What's next?

127
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,790
Do we have more orders?

128
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:19,790
No, only two.

129
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,000
In that case,

130
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,880
could you assist
one of the other artisans?

131
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:25,960
Oh, I could never do that.

132
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,670
It's their work, after all.

133
00:06:27,750 --> 00:06:29,580
[ANNE]
But it would be faster that way.

134
00:06:29,670 --> 00:06:32,790
It isn't right to interfere
with another person's work.

135
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,250
[gasps]

136
00:06:34,330 --> 00:06:35,250
[ANNE] I thought it was normal

137
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:37,460
for everyone in a workshop
to collaborate.

138
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:38,710
Uh...

139
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:41,790
[ANNE] Is there something
strange about what I said?

140
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:45,130
So, each of you completes
the task assigned to you

141
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:46,130
on your own?

142
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:48,330
Well, yes. We're artisans.

143
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,790
We take ownership of our work.

144
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:52,670
Then what
is the Head of Artisans

145
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:53,750
supposed to do?

146
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:57,380
[ORLAND] Manage the supply,
deal with clients,

147
00:06:57,460 --> 00:06:58,420
and of course,

148
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:00,210
you'll assess
every sugar confection

149
00:07:00,290 --> 00:07:01,290
that we produce

150
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:03,330
to determine
whether it might bring shame

151
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:05,290
upon the Paige Workshop.

152
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:06,630
Did you say shame?

153
00:07:07,290 --> 00:07:10,500
We can't deliver work that
tarnishes the name of Paige.

154
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:13,040
Therefore, it's imperative that
you have us make corrections

155
00:07:13,130 --> 00:07:14,540
if the product is lacking.

156
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:18,960
But, if the piece
is not an embarrassment,

157
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,330
you will approve it.

158
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:23,170
Then Mr. Glen will give it
the main workshop's seal.

159
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,210
That's your job
as Head of Artisans.

160
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:31,460
[ANNE] That's very different
from my experience so far.

161
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:32,540
How odd.

162
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:34,830
- Hello.
- [WOMAN] Hm?

163
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:38,080
Nice to meet you.
I'm Anne Halford.

164
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:40,750
Oh, hello there, miss.

165
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:43,710
My name is Dana
and this one's name is Hal.

166
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:46,920
You two look
practically identical!

167
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,830
- I imagine you must be siblings?
- [DANA] Yes.

168
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:52,080
Apparently, we were born
from the very same tree

169
00:07:52,170 --> 00:07:54,210
at the exact same moment,

170
00:07:54,290 --> 00:07:55,630
so in human terms,

171
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,460
I believe you would say
that we were twins.

172
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:58,420
[ANNE] Oh, really?

173
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:01,210
I didn't realize fairies
could be twins too!

174
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:02,880
Have you two had dinner yet?

175
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:05,000
I would be happy
to have you join me.

176
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:06,580
[DANA] Oh, no, we couldn't!

177
00:08:06,670 --> 00:08:09,210
This table is only
for artisans and family.

178
00:08:09,290 --> 00:08:11,080
[ANNE]
We all live in the same house!

179
00:08:11,170 --> 00:08:12,790
That's family enough, isn't it?

180
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:14,670
[DANA]
No, not in the slightest!

181
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:16,330
We're fairies, after all.

182
00:08:16,420 --> 00:08:17,420
Please excuse us!

183
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,080
- [ELLIOT] What a shame!
- [gasps]

184
00:08:23,750 --> 00:08:25,330
Turned you down, huh?

185
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:26,540
Mr. Collins.

186
00:08:26,630 --> 00:08:27,830
I'm sure you amazed everyone

187
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:29,330
on your first day
at the workshop.

188
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,880
So, what did you think of it,
Anne?

189
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:32,790
Hmm.

190
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:35,960
[ANNE] I learned a lot
about this place today.

191
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:38,670
The artisans make
what they want,

192
00:08:38,750 --> 00:08:40,330
and they don't help each other.

193
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:42,710
Everyone takes responsibility
for their own work.

194
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:46,130
That's how it's been at Paige
for 300 years now.

195
00:08:46,210 --> 00:08:48,080
Mr. Glen drills that
into all our heads

196
00:08:48,170 --> 00:08:49,500
more than anything else.

197
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:52,170
It sounds nice in theory,
except...

198
00:08:52,710 --> 00:08:53,540
Go on.

199
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:56,420
I don't know,
it just bothers me somehow.

200
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,330
[scoffs]

201
00:08:58,420 --> 00:09:01,750
Well, since I was the one
who put you in this position,

202
00:09:01,830 --> 00:09:02,670
got some time?

203
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:04,710
[thuds]

204
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:06,750
[ANNE] What's that?

205
00:09:06,830 --> 00:09:07,920
[ELLIOT] Promissory notes.

206
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
[ANNE] You mean debts?

207
00:09:09,630 --> 00:09:11,750
[ELLIOT] Right,
for about 10,000 cress,

208
00:09:11,830 --> 00:09:13,080
with this land as collateral.

209
00:09:13,170 --> 00:09:14,670
[ANNE] Did you say 10,000?

210
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:17,580
It's left over
from the last headmaster.

211
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:21,460
If it's not paid off this year,
we will lose half of this place.

212
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,290
[ANNE] Can you afford it?

213
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:24,210
No.

214
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:28,080
Which is why I went out to try
and negotiate again today.

215
00:09:28,170 --> 00:09:30,880
Oh, by the way, don't tell.

216
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:32,630
[ANNE] Don't tell Mr. Glen?

217
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:34,880
He knows we're in debt
obviously,

218
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:37,710
but not that we're having
a difficult time paying it back.

219
00:09:37,790 --> 00:09:39,580
And because of his illness,

220
00:09:39,670 --> 00:09:41,170
the lenders are becoming
concerned

221
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:43,130
about the future
of the workshop.

222
00:09:43,210 --> 00:09:44,290
That's awful.

223
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:47,960
You said earlier that something
didn't sit right with you.

224
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:49,420
[ANNE] I did.

225
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:52,380
[ELLIOT]
Well, I have opinions myself.

226
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:53,500
Huh?

227
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:56,710
None of us want
to turn our backs on Mr. Glen,

228
00:09:56,790 --> 00:09:58,460
but something's gone wrong here.

229
00:09:59,210 --> 00:10:00,540
I've given it a lot of thought,

230
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:03,460
and I still can't put my finger
on what the problem is.

231
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:07,170
Eh, I'll pay off
the debt somehow.

232
00:10:07,250 --> 00:10:10,040
As for you, Anne,
just do what you think is best

233
00:10:10,130 --> 00:10:11,920
like the first
silver sugar master.

234
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,580
You keep talking about that!

235
00:10:13,670 --> 00:10:15,290
What is it
you're trying to tell me?

236
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:22,000
[CHALLE] You're dining alone?
Why not join the others?

237
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,130
[BRIDGET] That's simple.

238
00:10:23,210 --> 00:10:25,460
I prefer to spend my time alone
with you.

239
00:10:26,170 --> 00:10:28,750
[CHALLE] And yet,
your expression looks lonely.

240
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:31,790
[BRIDGET] I'm not lonely at all.

241
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,290
Hold me, Challe.

242
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:44,290
♪

243
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,210
Carry me to bed.

244
00:10:51,580 --> 00:10:53,790
Now lay me down carefully.

245
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:55,080
Stroke my hair.

246
00:10:57,380 --> 00:10:59,080
Stay till I fall asleep.

247
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:02,130
Please don't go
to see that girl.

248
00:11:03,130 --> 00:11:05,080
Stay with me and only me.

249
00:11:22,710 --> 00:11:23,960
[door opens]

250
00:11:44,250 --> 00:11:45,420
- [CHALLE] Stare all you like...
- [gasps]

251
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:46,710
...nothing's going to happen.

252
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:48,250
[gasps]

253
00:11:49,710 --> 00:11:50,630
[screams]

254
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:52,920
You scared me!

255
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,880
I thought you couldn't sneak out

256
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:58,380
or Miss Bridget would make you
do more sordid things!

257
00:11:58,460 --> 00:11:59,580
- Sordid?
- Well,

258
00:11:59,670 --> 00:12:02,000
that's what Mythril Lid Pod
told me, anyway.

259
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:05,380
Mythril Lid Pod
has a wild imagination.

260
00:12:05,460 --> 00:12:07,460
She's a normal girl.

261
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:10,080
She's not forcing you
to do things?

262
00:12:10,170 --> 00:12:11,710
No, she's not.

263
00:12:12,210 --> 00:12:13,130
I'm so glad.

264
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:16,250
I'm going to work hard.

265
00:12:16,330 --> 00:12:17,790
Just hold on.

266
00:12:21,630 --> 00:12:25,460
♪

267
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:27,830
What... What's the matter?

268
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,170
Nothing.

269
00:12:29,710 --> 00:12:31,960
Are you forming an opinion
about all these?

270
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,710
[chuckles]

271
00:12:34,290 --> 00:12:36,040
Orland's work carries
a certain sense

272
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,960
of power and strength.

273
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,080
He's very quiet

274
00:12:39,170 --> 00:12:41,460
and a little hard to approach
sometimes

275
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:44,130
but I can tell he cares
about his creations.

276
00:12:46,330 --> 00:12:50,130
This one is by King,
who seems like a sincere person.

277
00:12:50,210 --> 00:12:52,920
He's awkward around women
for some reason, but...

278
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:57,580
his confections still have
such a romantic feeling to them!

279
00:12:57,670 --> 00:12:59,040
Don't you think it's beautiful?

280
00:13:01,170 --> 00:13:03,960
They've both done
excellent work,

281
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:06,750
but we've only got
these two commissions right now.

282
00:13:06,830 --> 00:13:09,080
I wonder why business
has gotten slow.

283
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:12,290
Hm? What's wrong?

284
00:13:13,630 --> 00:13:14,580
Nothing.

285
00:13:15,130 --> 00:13:16,670
- [door slams]
- [BRIDGET] Challe!

286
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,420
I asked you
not to see her again!

287
00:13:21,790 --> 00:13:24,330
You didn't ask for that,
you ordered,

288
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:26,380
and I don't intend to obey you.

289
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:27,630
Do what you must.

290
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:32,000
[BRIDGET] You're saying
you won't consider my feelings?

291
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:33,500
[CHALLE] You are my master now.

292
00:13:34,330 --> 00:13:36,290
And that means,
just as there's no expectation

293
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:38,080
for you to consider my feelings,

294
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:40,880
I can't think of any reason
to consider yours, either.

295
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:43,420
Is that so?

296
00:13:44,290 --> 00:13:45,420
Well then,

297
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,630
I suppose there's not
a single person in the world

298
00:13:47,710 --> 00:13:48,790
who cares how I feel.

299
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:52,080
[sniffles]
In that case...

300
00:13:53,630 --> 00:13:55,290
you are to be punished!

301
00:13:55,830 --> 00:13:57,750
- Wait!
- It's all right, Anne!

302
00:13:57,830 --> 00:14:00,920
No, Challe, I don't want
anything to happen to you!

303
00:14:02,830 --> 00:14:04,290
So meddlesome.

304
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:07,630
[panting]

305
00:14:07,710 --> 00:14:10,210
- [crashes]
- [Bridget sniffling]

306
00:14:13,670 --> 00:14:14,790
It's not here.

307
00:14:14,830 --> 00:14:19,380
[panting]

308
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:21,670
[BRIDGET] Only I know
about this hiding place.

309
00:14:21,750 --> 00:14:22,880
[Bridget sniffling]

310
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:26,630
So, who,
who could've stolen it?

311
00:14:26,710 --> 00:14:29,210
[ELLIOT] If you mean the wing,
Mr. Glen has it.

312
00:14:30,830 --> 00:14:31,920
[gasps]

313
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,420
What? Why is it with my father?

314
00:14:35,130 --> 00:14:36,710
[GLEN]
Bridget.

315
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:38,540
Listen, someone came

316
00:14:38,630 --> 00:14:40,710
and placed the wing
by my pillow,

317
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:41,960
so I'll say this now.

318
00:14:42,710 --> 00:14:45,500
Going forward,
the wing will remain in my care.

319
00:14:46,170 --> 00:14:49,960
Whoever left it with me probably
feels that it's for the best.

320
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:51,500
Why, Father?

321
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:53,380
You said it was all right
until I get married!

322
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:56,080
I can no longer tolerate
the way you're acting.

323
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,670
Locking that fairy in your room,

324
00:14:58,750 --> 00:15:01,460
forbidding that he spend time
with anyone but yourself.

325
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:04,880
Really, dear, it's as though
you've become obsessed!

326
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:05,880
[groans]

327
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:09,380
Bridget,
I beg you to be sensible!

328
00:15:09,710 --> 00:15:11,330
Whose daughter are you?

329
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:12,790
[Bridget sniffles]

330
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:14,500
I don't care!

331
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:19,540
Does this mean
that you're my new master?

332
00:15:19,630 --> 00:15:20,630
Yes, I am,

333
00:15:20,710 --> 00:15:25,040
and your orders are to interact
with Bridget in moderation.

334
00:15:25,130 --> 00:15:27,880
There's no need to respond
to her every demand,

335
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:30,290
but please don't do anything
that would hurt her.

336
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:32,000
But, Mr. Glen, Challe doesn't...

337
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:34,580
I will decide
what happens to him now.

338
00:15:35,630 --> 00:15:37,000
[Mythril gasps]

339
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,960
[MYTHRIL]
You actually got your wing back?

340
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:42,130
Not quite. It's just that
Mr. Glen has it instead of her.

341
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:43,670
[MYTHRIL] But you can go
where you please now!

342
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:45,790
What a torturous existence!

343
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,790
Letting that miserable woman
have her way with you,

344
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,000
all day and night!

345
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:51,380
Spare me
your moronic imaginings.

346
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:53,790
Well, we have a visitor,
so excuse me.

347
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:54,830
[MYTHRIL]
Right!

348
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:59,750
[GLEN] It's been
quite some time, Mr. Radcliffe.

349
00:15:59,830 --> 00:16:02,460
[ANNE]
Mr. Radcliffe and Keith?

350
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:05,460
I'm glad you're faring better
than the rumors would suggest.

351
00:16:05,540 --> 00:16:08,790
Oh, and, you've employed
a new silver sugar master.

352
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:10,130
[whimpers]

353
00:16:10,210 --> 00:16:12,250
This is our Head of Artisans, actually.

354
00:16:12,330 --> 00:16:13,420
Hm.

355
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,380
Judging by the timing
of her acceptance here,

356
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:17,920
are you taking part
in the selection

357
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,790
for
the Holy Beginnings Festival?

358
00:16:20,710 --> 00:16:22,210
[ANNE]
Hm? Selection?

359
00:16:22,290 --> 00:16:23,290
[GLEN]
Of course not.

360
00:16:23,380 --> 00:16:24,830
My father rejected it.

361
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:26,250
[MARCUS]
I see.

362
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:29,380
I had a suspicion
that that might be your answer.

363
00:16:30,210 --> 00:16:32,960
Ah, yes, and Powell's son
is here with me, as well.

364
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:35,330
My name is Keith, sir.

365
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:37,250
[GLEN]
I've heard talk about you.

366
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:39,500
They say
you've become a great artisan.

367
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:41,460
Thank you and I'm...

368
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:43,670
[sighs] sorry.

369
00:16:44,330 --> 00:16:45,670
There's no reason to be.

370
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:47,880
You chose your path.

371
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:49,580
[ANNE]
Keith.

372
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:51,630
[door opens]

373
00:16:52,130 --> 00:16:54,000
[ANNE]
I was surprised to see you!

374
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:57,330
[KEITH] Mr. Radcliffe
didn't give me much notice,

375
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:59,000
but I was wondering
how you've been doing.

376
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:02,790
Have you had any trouble, uh,
and how are things with Challe?

377
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:04,380
Oh, we're managing.

378
00:17:05,130 --> 00:17:06,080
What about with you?

379
00:17:06,170 --> 00:17:08,290
How are Kat and Jonas lately?

380
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:10,880
Actually, Mr. Hingley
has returned to his own shop.

381
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:15,670
Sadly, no one's been able
to get in touch with Jonas.

382
00:17:15,750 --> 00:17:17,920
He never went back
to his old hometown.

383
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,210
Oh, is that so?

384
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,460
By the way, Keith,

385
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:22,920
can you tell me
about the selection

386
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,500
for
the Holy Beginnings Festival?

387
00:17:25,380 --> 00:17:27,710
[KEITH] It's part
of the new-year celebrations.

388
00:17:27,790 --> 00:17:30,040
As you know,
they set out sugar confections

389
00:17:30,130 --> 00:17:32,040
in the Church
of Saint Lewiston Bell.

390
00:17:32,130 --> 00:17:34,710
Workshops create
the sample pieces for it,

391
00:17:34,790 --> 00:17:37,670
and one of them is selected
to produce the work that year.

392
00:17:37,750 --> 00:17:38,880
[ANNE]
Oh, I see.

393
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:41,210
[KEITH]
It's a great honor to be picked,

394
00:17:41,290 --> 00:17:44,080
and if the school successfully
delivers all the pieces,

395
00:17:44,170 --> 00:17:45,380
the kingdom's religion awards

396
00:17:45,460 --> 00:17:46,880
- 10,000 cress.
- [Anne gasps]

397
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:50,380
[KEITH] Then naturally,
that school becomes popular,

398
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:51,960
and more commissions come in.

399
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,920
Oh, it looks like
she has company.

400
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,630
- Her lover?
- Nadir!

401
00:17:56,710 --> 00:17:58,250
It's nothing of the sort!

402
00:17:58,330 --> 00:18:00,630
Don't say such awful things
to him!

403
00:18:00,710 --> 00:18:02,460
Oh, there's nothing awful
about that.

404
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:03,380
Huh?

405
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:05,330
Oh.

406
00:18:06,830 --> 00:18:09,420
I'm Keith Powell
of the Radcliffe Workshop.

407
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:12,330
Ah! So, you're him?

408
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:13,630
Yes, I understand.

409
00:18:13,710 --> 00:18:15,420
Feel free to stay, then.

410
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:16,420
We should go.

411
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:17,330
[NADIR] Hm?

412
00:18:18,210 --> 00:18:21,710
But... Well, um, bye!

413
00:18:22,670 --> 00:18:24,040
Why'd they rush off?

414
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,000
[KEITH]
They had to,

415
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:29,290
because from their perspective,
I'm a traitor.

416
00:18:29,380 --> 00:18:30,500
[ANNE] What do you mean?

417
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:31,420
♪

418
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:33,630
[KEITH] My father became
the Silver Sugar Viscount

419
00:18:33,710 --> 00:18:35,960
while he was
with the Paige Workshop.

420
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,830
It really invigorated
this place.

421
00:18:38,790 --> 00:18:41,460
So, after he passed away,

422
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:43,670
naturally, everyone assumed
that I would come to Paige

423
00:18:43,750 --> 00:18:44,960
as he had done,

424
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:47,500
but in the end,
I chose the Radcliffe Workshop.

425
00:18:48,250 --> 00:18:50,710
And then,
the rumor went around, saying,

426
00:18:50,790 --> 00:18:53,000
"Powell has given up on Paige."

427
00:18:54,210 --> 00:18:55,880
That caused the artisans
who worked here

428
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:58,960
to begin transferring
to other schools all at once.

429
00:19:01,580 --> 00:19:03,210
That's just terrible.

430
00:19:03,290 --> 00:19:07,250
But the truth is,
I hadn't given up on this place.

431
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:09,750
If I'd come here,

432
00:19:09,830 --> 00:19:12,580
I would've been affected
by my father's influence.

433
00:19:12,670 --> 00:19:15,580
I didn't want to follow
in his footsteps.

434
00:19:15,670 --> 00:19:17,210
That was the only reason.

435
00:19:17,290 --> 00:19:19,790
I endured it
while he held his position,

436
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:22,380
but even still, after he died,

437
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:23,540
I resented the idea

438
00:19:23,630 --> 00:19:25,710
of being seen
as the son of Edward Powell.

439
00:19:26,250 --> 00:19:29,670
The name Keith Powell
means something on its own.

440
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,630
- Don't worry.
- Hm.

441
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:35,290
It's not your fault

442
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:37,880
that the Paige Workshop
ended up this way,

443
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:39,580
and everyone here knows that.

444
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:42,830
But their feelings haven't
caught up yet, that's all.

445
00:19:43,710 --> 00:19:46,290
Given some time,
that resentment will go away.

446
00:19:46,380 --> 00:19:49,420
♪

447
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,750
[KEITH]
Thank you, Anne. Truly.

448
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:57,040
[ANNE] If we can turn
this place around,

449
00:19:57,130 --> 00:19:59,750
then maybe Keith
will stop blaming himself,

450
00:19:59,830 --> 00:20:01,670
and the artisans
will accept him again.

451
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:04,080
I have to succeed!

452
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:06,460
[MARCUS]
Keith! It's time!

453
00:20:06,540 --> 00:20:07,380
[KEITH]
Right!

454
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:09,790
We're leaving so soon?

455
00:20:10,630 --> 00:20:12,790
I wonder
if Mr. Radcliffe is worried.

456
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:14,710
The selection's
only half a month away.

457
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:16,500
[ANNE]
The selection.

458
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:18,920
- Oh, wait, that's it!
- [gasps]

459
00:20:20,250 --> 00:20:21,130
Uh?

460
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:23,250
Thank you so much!

461
00:20:23,330 --> 00:20:24,790
Of course.

462
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:27,380
I'm not too certain
what I did for you,

463
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,460
but still, you're very welcome.

464
00:20:30,210 --> 00:20:33,420
[ANNE] Yes, if we win,
more people will notice us.

465
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:35,960
And we'll get 10,000 cress!

466
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:37,880
What Mr. Collins said,

467
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:40,420
and the things
that were weighing on my mind,

468
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:41,790
it could be!

469
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:43,000
[knocking on door]

470
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:44,080
I have a request.

471
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,540
I would like for our workshop
to take part

472
00:20:46,630 --> 00:20:48,420
in this year's
festival selection.

473
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:50,880
If we do, it might help us
return to our former--

474
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:51,920
[GLEN]
No.

475
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:52,830
[gasps]

476
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
We will not participate.

477
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:57,000
[gasps]

478
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,130
But, sir...

479
00:21:04,170 --> 00:21:09,170
♪

